SysPulse Native R11 Linux administration evaluation. Coexists with Alpha 39.
Run as an ordinary desktop account, not root. Reviewed APT upgrades and repair
require matching successful preview and separate authorization. APT takes its
own transaction locks after the helper rechecks the plan; a race remains.
System and user service changes, Wi-Fi and power profiles require review.
System service stop/restart excludes selected foundational service names; this
is not a complete dependency or alias safety analysis. Offline ext filesystem
check/repair requires UDisks2 and gdbus, matching unmounted device identity,
unique UUID, a failed check before repair and separate backup confirmation.
UDisks performs authorization and its own mount checks. No forced unmount.
No firewall mutation. Optional tools may be absent; operations then fail closed.
Actual privileged service, package, memory, TRIM and filesystem mutations and
NetworkManager/power daemon changes have NOT been verified on a real Mint
session. Keep Alpha 39 installed. Unsigned evaluation; full parity, Windows
and signed update pending. No background update or maintenance is installed.
R11 adds actual ordinary-user verified single-file copy and restore to a NEW
path (64 MiB maximum, private mode 0600, no symlinks, no overwrite). It is not
recursive backup, metadata preservation, snapshot or recovery of deleted data.
The destination filesystem must support hardlinks; same-user races remain.
Live CPU and RAM history added. Full replacement remains unaccepted.
Desktop / reports adds optional native desktop tool launchers (not internal
implementations of those tools) and an explicit redacted local report export.
Reports are saved in the owned account home with private permissions, no
overwrite. External tool execution not tested in the current environment.
